WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.661 --> 00:00:07.441
Today I'm going to show you how
to create bottle label mockup

00:00:07.441 --> 00:00:11.281
in Adobe Photoshop. First open
your rectangle tool from the

00:00:11.281 --> 00:00:15.841
toolbar and draw a rectangle.
Now click the fill color and

00:00:15.841 --> 00:00:19.281
choose any color for shape.
Then close properties. Right

00:00:19.281 --> 00:00:22.481
click and convert it to smart
object. And then decrease the

00:00:22.481 --> 00:00:26.481
opacity. Press "Ctrl+T" to
free transform. Then right

00:00:26.481 --> 00:00:30.481
click and choose the distort.
Click and drag of the corner

00:00:30.481 --> 00:00:37.181
handles. Right click again and
choose warp. Now use these

00:00:37.181 --> 00:00:39.901
handles to distort the shape
and match it to your bottle's

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.221
body.

00:00:43.661 --> 00:00:49.821
Hit "Enter" when you're finished.
Double click on this and rename

00:00:49.821 --> 00:00:54.461
it your image. Set the opacity
back to 100%. Then right

00:00:54.461 --> 00:00:58.221
click in group from layers. I'm
going to name this design. Then

00:00:58.221 --> 00:01:01.981
click okay. Disable the group
layer. Select the background.

00:01:01.981 --> 00:01:05.341
Open your quick selection tool
from the toolbar. And click and

00:01:05.341 --> 00:01:08.301
drag over the bottle label to
select it. Enable the group

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:11.821
layer. Then create a layer
mask. Let's place the design of

00:01:11.821 --> 00:01:15.261
the bottle by double clicking
on the thumbnail. Now go to

00:01:15.261 --> 00:01:19.101
file. Place embedded and place
your label design. Adjust the

00:01:19.101 --> 00:01:24.221
size position. Hit "Enter" once
you're satisfied. Go back to

00:01:24.221 --> 00:01:28.701
file and choose save. And then
close the document. Select the

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:31.581
group layer. Change the blend
mode of this layer from normal

00:01:31.581 --> 00:01:35.581
to linear burn. Click the FX
icon and choose the blending

00:01:35.581 --> 00:01:39.021
options. Hold the "Alt" key and
then use these sliders to

00:01:39.021 --> 00:01:44.601
adjust the shadows in
highlights. Click okay once

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:51.321
you're satisfied. And that's
it. Thanks for watching.

